o  and then use an instant thermometer to  take it off  and so what you're going to do the most  important thing that i have to tell you  is i'm going to take this  marinade and i'm going to pour it into  the pot that i took  everything out of and when i take the  steaks  off the grill once i turn them i'm going  to put them back in this marinade  and it it will take about 15 minutes for  the juices to all settle  get back into the meat and also for the  marinade  which i do at at the end of cooking when  it's resting  and talking about resting cooking alex  if you're cooking medium rare steaks to  130 degrees  take them off the grill at 125 degrees  because when you put them in and put the  top on  to rest they come up five sec five  degrees  and the other tip i want to give you yes  and so you can  undercook everything about five degrees  the other thing is you don't want to oh  here we've got a flame  you don't want to do something that i  have always done which is compressing  the meat  which we all love for that flame to come  up  um but don't do that because you're  taking the fat and draining it out  and that's it that's all the tips for  cooking and grilling  that you need for a friday afternoon and  it was a pleasure doing business with  you alex i look forward to seeing  you yeah yet again yes oh my gosh thank  you so much you made that look so easy  nanny bubbe thank you  and you can check more out on nanny  bubby's kitchen and garden on social  media  and online at nannybuffy.com thank you  so much that was a great show and tell  that's something hopefully we can  replicate at home also want to say a big  thank you to chapman automotive for  sponsoring  this segment

